- Admin sets ONE base currency ([BASE CURRENCY]) in which prices are entered. All visitor prices are converted from the base currency using live exchange rates (open.er-api.com or exchangerate.host). Cache rates in Firestore (settings/exchangeRates), refresh via scheduled Cloud Function every 12 hours; frontend falls back to cached rates if the API fails.
- Format with Intl.NumberFormat using the correct symbol and locale (₹1,999, $24.99, £19.99, €22,50). Handle zero-decimal currencies (JPY). Optional admin setting for price rounding (.99 style or clean numbers).
- Header and footer contain a "Region and currency" selector (flag + country + currency code) to manually change country, currency and language. Save in localStorage and in the customer profile when logged in.
- Currency change applies instantly everywhere (grid, product page, cart, checkout, sale prices, shipping fees) without reload. On checkout, show a note when charged currency differs: "Prices shown in [currency]. You will be charged in [charged currency]".
- Payment currency logic: charge in the visitor's currency if the active gateway supports it (Stripe, PayPal, Razorpay International), otherwise charge in the base currency and show the converted amount. Store in every order: displayCurrency, chargedCurrency, exchangeRateUsed, totals in both currencies.
